## Grill (locked answers — do not re-litigate)

| Challenge | Verdict |
| :--- | :--- |
| Hover actions in-flow vs overlay? | **Out-of-flow overlay.** Today `CalendarView` mounts `mt-auto pt-1 flex flex-col gap-1` **inside** the day cell (`h-auto min-h-[128px]`). Those `h-7 w-full` buttons add in-flow height; the CSS-grid week row grows; neighbors stretch. Hover **must not** change the day cell’s used layout size. Neighboring days stay aligned. |
| Overlay vs portal? | **`position: absolute` child of the day cell** (cell is already `relative`). Absolute / fixed children do not contribute to grid row height. Keep the existing cell `onMouseEnter` / `onMouseLeave` so moving onto the actions does not dismiss. A **portal is allowed only** if a pointer-bridge prevents `mouseleave` from closing when the pointer is on the popover. Default: in-cell absolute. `overflow: visible` on the cell; the menu may paint over adjacent days. **Forbidden:** in-flow `mt-auto` stacks, `h-auto` growth from buttons, MUI/shadcn/Radix Popover. |
| Smaller than today’s buttons? | **Yes.** Today: full-width `h-7` primary slabs. Overlay is `width: max-content` (cap ~160px, not `w-full`), actions `h-6` / `text-[10px]–[11px]`, stacked compact. New session stays the one filled `#007AFF` action; Copy to and Notes are secondary (`bg-white/15` or text). Do not duplicate the screenshot’s large stacked CTAs. |
| Empty day vs day with sessions? | **Empty:** overlay = **New session** + **Notes**. No Copy to. Empty-day **click** still opens New session (unchanged). **Has ≥1 session:** overlay = **New session** + **Copy to** + **Notes**. Copy to still uses `dayWorkouts[0]` / existing clipboard rules. Copy-to mode hides the overlay (unchanged). Coach with no athlete: no overlay (`calendar-empty`). |
| One note vs many? | **One `DayNote` per `(owner_id, date)`.** One card on that calendar day. Hover **Notes** and click-the-card edit the same document. Extra paragraphs go in that body. Do not stack many note cards. Saving empty / whitespace **tombstones** the row; the card disappears. |
| Click note card vs hover Notes? | **Same editor** (`CenteredDialog`, title `Notes · YYYY-MM-DD`, no duplicate date field). Click note card: `stopPropagation`, open editor — **never** open a session. Hover **Notes**: create if none, else edit. Click session card: still opens the session. Click empty padding on a day with a note: still New session only when there are **zero** sessions (same as today). |
| Overlay vs rest card? | Overlay = **actions only** (no textarea in the hover menu). The note **card is visible at rest**, not hover-only. Resting content (sessions + note card) **may** grow the cell; that is real data, like extra sessions. Hover chrome must not. |
| Coach vs athlete? | **Same calendar UI.** Notes live in **athlete plan space** (`planAthleteId`). Linked coach has shared full write; unlink revokes access only; notes stay with the athlete. Coach without selected athlete: existing empty state, no hover, no notes fetch. RBAC matches sessions (`athlete_id` query, ended links blocked). |
| Reuse set notes / workout notes / vs-note? | **No existing day-note store.** Repo search: `ExerciseSet.note` (Telegram micro-note), analytics `coaching_notes`, Sheets prose “session notes” with **no Workout column**. **No** `DayNote`, **no** `vs-note` component. Do **not** stuff day text into `ExerciseSet.note`, `Workout.title`, or `InsightCard`. **First** store: new `DayNote`. Not a second store. |
| Date vs weekday vs session? | **Per calendar date** (`YYYY-MM-DD`) on the athlete plan. Not Mon–Sun containers, not `dayLabel`, not attached to a Workout (notes may exist on a day with zero sessions). Calendar stays date-first. |
| Copy-to D1? | **Unchanged.** Destination click = earliest source **date** (`copyClipboard.ts` `dateOffsetDays`). Not `workout.dayLabel`. Copy copies **sessions**, not day notes. Notes stay on the source date. |
| Telegram / Sheets / demo / nested cards? | Unchanged unless notes already publish — they **do not**. Do not add a Sheets tab or Telegram command this pass. No demo seed. Note card is a **sibling** of session chips in the cell, not nested inside `workout-card`. No MUI/shadcn. |

