## Spec

### Hover overlay (layout)

- Mount only when `hoveredDate === dateStr` && current month && athlete selected && `!copyClipboard`.
- **Out of flow:** `absolute` (e.g. bottom-center of the cell). Must not participate in the cell’s in-flow height. Week row height with overlay open **equals** the same week with overlay closed (e2e: `boundingBox` of hovered day vs neighbor, and/or hovered day height before vs after hover).
- **Smaller** than today’s full-width `h-7` stack (see grill).
- Actions, top to bottom: **New session** (always) → **Copy to** (iff a session exists) → **Notes** (always).
- `data-testid`: keep `calendar-new-session-{date}` and `calendar-copy-to-{workoutId}`; add `calendar-notes-{date}`.
- Existing click-day / click-session / copy-to-banner behavior stays.

### Note card (rest)

- If a non-tombstoned `DayNote` exists for that `dateStr`, render a card in the cell **without hover**.
- Distinct from session cards: no SQ/BP/DL load line; muted surface; label **Note**; 2-line truncated body.
- Place **after** session chips (date header → sessions → note). Empty day with only a note: date → note card.
- `data-testid="day-note-card-{date}"`. Click opens the editor; `stopPropagation`.
- Not nested inside `workout-card`. No decorative hero.

### Editor

- Reuse `CenteredDialog`. Title `Notes · YYYY-MM-DD`. Body: one textarea (`data-testid="day-note-body"`), freeform text (not a prescription parser). Cap **2000** chars.
- Footer: Cancel / Save. Empty save deletes (tombstone) and closes.
- Offline: disable Save; copy **Connect to save notes.** (same idea as Copy to).
- Loading / error / permission-denied visible. Locked/conflict: N/A unless a workout lock is later reused — **do not** require `WorkoutLock` for a date with no session.

### Data model (new, one store)

`DayNote`: `id`, `owner_id` (athlete), `date` (`YYYY-MM-DD`), `body` (text), `updated_at`, `deleted_at`. Unique `(owner_id, date)` among live rows.

- Athlete-owned plan; linked coach shared write; ended link → 403.
- REST: list/upsert/delete scoped like `/api/microcycles?athlete_id=`. Upsert is **idempotent** on `(owner_id, date)`.
- Fetch with the plan (PeriodizationContext snapshot **or** sibling list loaded in `CalendarView`). Do not use LocalStorage. IndexedDB snapshot of notes is OK if the plan snapshot already works that way; canonical writes are backend.
- Do **not** add `mutation_type: day_note` to workout sync this pass (workout sync still needs `workout_id`). Do not fake a workout to attach a note.

### Out of scope

- Sessions view note list; Insights; Telegram; Sheets publish of notes
- Copying notes; weekday note columns; set micro-notes UI on web
- Demo seed; nested cards; MUI/shadcn

